    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0388" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg384"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.1153 Smith Company, Werner G./18:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-29T16:00:00-04:00">June 29, 1938—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>408. Following for Tokyo: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“220 June 29, 4 p.m. Your 391, June 20, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="95"
                                xml:id="d511-f1"/> and Nanking’s 127, June 27, 4 p.m.<anchor n="96"
                                xml:id="d511-f2"/> (which Shanghai has been requested to repeat to
                            you) in regard to wood oil of Werner G. Smith.</p>
                        <pb facs="0389" n="385" xml:id="pg385"/>
                        <p>The Department desires that, in such manner as you deem appropriate, you
                            ask the Foreign Office whether any reports of the investigation promised
                            have been received and express your Government’s increasing concern over
                            the continued delay in the release of the wood oil.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Please repeat to Tokyo Nanking’s 127, June 27, 4 p.m., and inform Nanking of
                    action taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d511-f1" n="95" xml:id="d511-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 873, June 20, 7 p.m., from the Consul General at Shanghai, <ref
                        target="#pg367">p. 367</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d511-f2" n="96" xml:id="d511-f2-content">
